          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Gel’fand triple
            is a structure that equips a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            with a dense
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector subspace
            of good “test” functions, so that the dual of the subspace of test functions enhaces the Hilbert space by embedding it into a larger
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} TVS
            whose elements can be considered as generalized
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eigenvector"} eigenvector
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+an+operator"} spectrum
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+operator"} normal
            (possibly
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unbounded+operator"} unbounded
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear operator
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong Gel’fand triple
            is datum of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_1.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi J
                  %mi H
                  %mover
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  B\stackrel{J}\hookrightarrow H \stackrel{K}\hookrightarrow B^*
          %p
            where
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_2.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+Hilbert+space"} separable Hilbert space
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_3.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+space"} Banach space
            (or more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
            (TVS)),
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_4.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^*
            is a dual TVS of
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_5.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_6.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J:B\hookrightarrow H
            is an injective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+operator"} bounded operator
            with dense image, and
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_7.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is the composition of the canonical isomorphism
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_8.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ≅
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\cong H^*
            determined by the inner product (i.e. given by Riesz theorem) and of the Banach transpose (dual)
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_9.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^*: H^*\to B^*
            of the operator
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_10.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_11.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J(B)
            is dense in
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_12.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            implies that
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_13.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi J
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J^*
            (hence also
            = succeed ")" do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_14.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %h2#basic_examples Basic examples
          %p
            A typical example is
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_15.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B = \mathcal{S}(\mathbb{R}^n)
            (Schwarz space),
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_16.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = L^2(\mathbb{R}^n)
            and
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_17.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo *
                  %mo =
                  %mi 𝒮
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^* = \mathcal{S}'(\mathbb{R}^n)
            (the space of tempered (Schwarz) distributions). One of the basic facts on Fourier transform is that this Gel’fand triple is preserved by the Fourier transform.
          %p
            Another natural example is
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_18.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝓁
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝓁
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝓁
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{l}^1\hookrightarrow \mathcal{l}^2\hookrightarrow \mathcal{l}^\infty
          %h4#a_long_example A long example
          %p
            Let
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_19.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            be the Hilbert space
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_20.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^2(\mathbb{R}, d x)
            consisting of square integrable functions
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_21.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            with respect to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lebesgue+measure"} Lebesgue measure
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_22.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi H
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                  %mo :
                  %mi f
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x: H \to H: f \mapsto x \cdot f
          %p
            where
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_23.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi y
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x \cdot f)(y) := y f(y)
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_24.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_25.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_26.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is the Schwartz space consisting of smooth functions
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_27.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            on
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_28.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            all of whose derivatives
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_29.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{(n)}(x)
            decay rapidly at infinity (more rapidly than any negative power of
            = succeed ")," do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_30.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |x|
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_31.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi S
                    %mo →
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: S \to H
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_32.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x
            is defined globally on
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_33.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %p
            Meanwhile the Schwartz space
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_34.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            carries its own topology (as described in the article
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distribution"} distribution
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_35.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_36.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^*
            is defined to be the continuous dual of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} TVS
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_37.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_38.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: S \to H
            is dense, it follows that any continuous functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_39.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: S \to \mathbb{C}
          %p
            has at most one extension to a continuous functional
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_40.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \to \mathbb{C}
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_41.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi i
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i^*: H^* \to S^*
          %p
            is injective. In addition, the topology on
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_42.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is such that the operator
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_43.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x: S \to S
            is continuous.
          %p
            In this example, there is a dense inclusion
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_44.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to S^*
            defined by the inner product pairing, and the operator
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x
            extends uniquely to an operator
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^* \to S^*
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x
            by abuse of notation. Again, in this example, the operator
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_48.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x: S^* \to S^*
            has an eigenvector
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_49.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi ξ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_{\xi}
            for each
            = succeed ":" do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_50.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi \in \mathbb{R}
          .maruku-equation
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_51.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi m
                    %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi ξ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ξ
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi ξ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m_x(s_{\xi}) = \xi s_{\xi}
          %p (under construction)
          %h2#isomorphisms Isomorphisms
          %p
            An isomorphism of Gelfand triples
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_52.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 1
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 2
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B_1,H_1,B^*_1)\to (B_2,H_2,B^*_2)
            is a unitary isomorphism
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_53.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_1\to H_2
            which restricts to an isomorphism of Banach spaces
            = succeed "," do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_54.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_1\to B_2
            = succeed "-" do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_55.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            = succeed "." do
              %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_56.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 1
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 2
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_1^*\to B_2^*
          %h2#terminology_and_references Terminology and references
          %h4#terminological_variants_and_history Terminological variants and history
          %p
            Usually,
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_57.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and
            %math#mathml_e7e37c25f259f3d3fec879046ff140382a3a44c3_58.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B^*
            are Banach spaces, when we say
            = succeed "," do
              %em Banach Gel’fand triple
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
            = succeed "," do
              %em rigged Hilbert space
            %em enriched
            Hilbert space is used (оснащенное гильбертово пространство), sometimes translated also as
            %em equipped
            Hilbert space. The enriched word here is the same as in the phrase
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
          %h4#early_references Early references
          %p Gel’fand triples were introduced by Gel’fand school about 1955 and quickly incorporated into the theory of generalized functions.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                [[I. M. Gelʹfand, A. G. Kostyučenko,
                %em
